#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "customer.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki to Customer Account Admin Permissions
	Testing to assure that customer account admin permissions work properly.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I generate static mmddyyyy start and end dates
	* I generate static full start and end dates
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | cstm.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | cstm.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | CSTM                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                            |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | cstm.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | cstm.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | CSTM                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                            |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | KORCSTKORCST                  | |
	| Name   | Korcst - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region | United States                 | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	| Tier   | T1                            | |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "cstm.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Requester |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "cstm.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support User |

Teardown:
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| CSTM Customer |
	* I tear down the product consumption list on koroneiki made by the account "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production      |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production      |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| KORCSTKORCST |
	| KORCT2KORCT2 |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korcst - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| KORCSTKORCST |
	| KORCT2KORCT2 |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| cstm.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| cstm.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| cstm.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| cstm.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| cstm.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| cstm.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| cstm.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| cstm.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| cstm.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| cstm.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |

Scenario: View DXP Production account on Customer project page as an admin
	Testing the ability to create a DXP Production project in Koroneiki and viewing the project in Customer projects page

	Given I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korcst"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I click on the Sync To Customer Portal button on the account page
	And I log into the customer homepage as "${staticCustomerAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticCustomerAdminPassword}"
	And I search the customer projects page using the keyword "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I click on the project with the name "Korcst - ${staticProjectName}" on the customer project details page
	Then I should be able to view a support level purchase on the customer subscription page with the following values 
	| Name                    | Platinum                                                      |
	| Status                  | CURRENT                                                       |
	| Support Level Duration  | ${staticMmDdYyyyStartDate} - ${staticMmDdYyyyOriginalEndDate} |
	And I filter the subscriptions details page to show only "Active" subscriptions
	And I filter the subscriptions details page to show only subscriptions related to "DXP"
	And I should be able to view a "Production" subscription purchase on the customer project overview page with the following values
	| Type                   | DXP                                                           |
	| Name                   | Production                                                    |
	| Date                   | ${staticMmDdYyyyStartDate} - ${staticMmDdYyyyOriginalEndDate} |
	| Instance Size          | 1                                                             |
	| State                  | Active                                                        |